  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2015) position from Midland Bank's own audited annual report \"MDB Financial Performance and Ratios: 5 Years Overview\", taken from the FY2015 report (the reporting year's own document). SOLO / STANDALONE basis. Midland Bank was licensed in 2013, so FY2013 is the bank's first year of operation and this series covers its entire public history; there is no FY2011 or FY2012 to report. All figures are as reported by the bank; the source table prints total liabilities directly, so nothing on the balance sheet is derived. The row mapped to operating_profit is the bank's 'Profit before provision and tax' (labelled 'Profit before provision on loans and corporate tax' in some years), i.e. pre-provision operating profit. The NPL ratio was read directly from the FY2017 report's 'NPL to total loans and advances (%)' row rather than parsed, because the dashes printed for FY2013-FY2014 leave that row with fewer numbers than year columns. The FY2016 report agrees on FY2015 and FY2016, and the FY2021 report agrees on FY2017. RESTATEMENTS -- 7 figure(s) here are reported differently by other Midland Bank annual reports; the contemporaneous value is kept and the divergence recorded: operating_expenses: this record uses 655.03 (AR2015); AR2016 report 611; operating_profit: this record uses 775.4 (AR2015); AR2016 report 819; profit_before_tax: this record uses 630.33 (AR2015); AR2016 report 674; profit_after_tax: this record uses 438.82 (AR2015); AR2016 report 483; nav_per_share: this record uses 12.67 (AR2015); AR2016 report 11.73; roa_pct: this record uses 1.84 (AR2015); AR2016 report 2.48; roe_pct: this record uses 8.63 (AR2015); AR2016 report 10.59. Classified loans are calculated as the reported NPL percentage applied to reported loans and advances, because the source table prints the ratio but not the absolute figure for most years. The provision charge for the year is calculated as profit before provision and tax minus profit after provision before tax; the source table's own provision row wraps across two lines and its label is lost in text extraction in several reports. The derivation reproduces the printed figure exactly where it is readable (FY2025: 2,702 - 1,110 = 1,592; FY2024: 2,114 - 1,125 = 989; FY2023: 1,743 - 1,277 = 466).",
